    "advancement": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>6th-level Study of Frost feature</em></p><p>Whenever a creature takes cold damage from one of your mage spells, its movement speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of your next turn.</p><p>When a creature has its speed reduced in this way, you can spend one sorcery point to force that creature to make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, that creature is restrained for 1 minute or until a creature lands a hit against it.</p><p>Beginning at 14th level, a creature who fails the saving throw is paralyzed instead of restrained.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
